\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Proposition}
\title{Independence from every translation link}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{Fix the entire collection #{R=(R_i(x))} of rotational links
on the \vocabk{rotational cochains}{fdip-00YN}. Changing the
translation collection from #{a} to #{a'} preserves each of #{\extd_R,\extdag_R,\extD_R,\cov_R}.
Whenever the cochain module is finite free, each of the two
determinants #{\det(m\bbI+\extD_R)} and #{\det(m\bbI+\cov_R)}
has the same value at #{a} as at #{a'}, for every scalar #{m\in k}.}

\proof{
\p{Every coefficient of #{T_i^R} and its inverse in
the [rotation-only formulas](fdip-00YO) depends only on #{A(R_i(x))} or its inverse.
The cubical insertion and deletion maps are fixed. Substitution in
the raising and lowering sums shows that neither depends on
#{a}. Their sum and their difference therefore depend only on
#{R}. For either choice, adding #{m\bbI} gives the same
endomorphism at #{a} and #{a'}, hence the same determinant.}
}

\p{Fixing the entire link collection is stronger than fixing
only the rotational holonomy of one plaquette. The assertion uses
the former condition.}
